# Input Event UI Root Resolution Implementation Plan

Source proposals: `Docs/input-event-ui-root-resolution-proposal.md` and
`Docs/input-event-service-proposal.md`

## Goal

Replace provisional UI-root adaptation and duplicated pointer-hit logic with
explicit root descriptors and shared obstruction classifiers. Preserve the
public Input Event API, existing hook ownership, pointer-policy semantics, and
RAW/predecessor/MAP ordering while making `MAP_CLICK` require determinate proof
that no supported interactive UI element obstructed the sampled screen point.

## Assumptions and constraints

- The approved proposals are authoritative; this plan does not redesign the
  public `observe(event_type, callback)` or `intercept(event_type, handler)` API.
- The existing input trampoline remains the sole hook. No second trampoline or
  native-to-`gui.View` adaptation is introduced.
- `RAW_CLICK` does not require UI-resolution success. `MAP_CLICK` is suppressed
  by `TARGET`, `BLOCKED`, `UNKNOWN`, or overlay-predecessor consumption.
- Existing `PointerPolicy` continues to configure pointer behavior;
  `PointerClassificationKind` represents the resolved result.
- Native interaction recognition is intentionally heuristic. Unrecognized
  native widgets are not hits merely because they occupy visible geometry.
- `GLOBAL_POSITIONING` is treated as absolute screen space; other native widget
  origins are parent-relative. Native automation must qualify this assumption.
- Root collection is shallow. Classifiers own visibility, activity, geometry,
  clipping, traversal, and pointer-policy evaluation.
- All production classes and methods require LuaDoc, new production modules are
  reload-managed in dependency order, and closed discriminators use immutable
  numeric enums.

## Phase 1: Establish generic position and canonical classification contracts

Outcome: All pointer-resolution work can target one validated immutable result
shape without introducing parallel coordinate or outcome types.

- [x] Rename the immutable `ScreenPosition` value type to `Position2D`.
  - [x] Update declarations, constructors, exports, and direct consumers.
  - [x] Preserve copied immutable `{x, y}` validation and behavior.
- [x] Rename the immutable `MapTilePosition` value type to `Position3D`.
  - [x] Update declarations, constructors, exports, and direct consumers.
  - [x] Preserve copied immutable `{x, y, z}` validation and behavior.
- [x] Ensure field names, not the generic value types, identify coordinate
  space: `screen_position`, `map_position`, and `local_position`.
- [x] Introduce immutable numeric `PointerClassificationKind` members:
  `TARGET`, `BLOCKED`, `MISS`, and `UNKNOWN`.
- [x] Introduce the immutable canonical classification result with fields
  `kind`, `subject`, and `local_position`.
  - [x] Require `subject` and `local_position` for `TARGET`.
  - [x] Require `subject` and forbid `local_position` for `BLOCKED`.
  - [x] Forbid both optional fields for `MISS` and `UNKNOWN`.
- [x] Add focused tests for generic position immutability, copied values,
  canonical result immutability, and every result invariant.

Completion criteria:

- [x] Generic position and canonical classification contracts are available to
  later migrations without separate axis fields or coordinate-space labels.
- [x] Invalid canonical result shapes are rejected by focused tests.

## Phase 2: Introduce the shared classifier invocation boundary

Outcome: GUI and native classifiers share one non-throwing, result-validating
entry point with consistent diagnostics and `UNKNOWN` fallback behavior.

- [x] Add the `PointerObstructionClassifier` base class.
  - [x] Expose the public final-style `invoke(root, screen_position)` method.
  - [x] Define protected `_classify(root, screen_position)` for subclasses.
  - [x] Validate inputs before invoking subclass behavior.
  - [x] Catch classifier exceptions, record private diagnostics, and return a
    canonical immutable `UNKNOWN` result.
  - [x] Validate subclass results and convert malformed results to `UNKNOWN`.
- [x] Ensure diagnostics distinguish invocation failure from a valid positive
  obstruction without retaining mutable roots.
- [x] Add focused tests for valid results, input validation, exception
  containment, malformed-result conversion, and diagnostic recording.

Completion criteria:

- [x] Every classifier failure is contained at `invoke()` and represented as
  canonical `UNKNOWN`.
- [x] Callers can rely on one immutable result contract and never call
  `_classify()` directly.

## Phase 3: Extract GUI-view classification from PointerDispatcher

Outcome: GUI-view obstruction policy has one implementation shared by
continuous pointer lifecycle and Input Event obstruction resolution.

- [x] Add `GuiViewPointerObstructionClassifier` as a
  `PointerObstructionClassifier` subclass.
- [x] Move current `gui.View` activity, visibility, frame, clipping, child
  traversal, and `PointerPolicy` resolution out of `PointerDispatcher`.
- [x] Preserve front-to-back traversal and existing `TARGET`, `PASS`, `BLOCK`,
  and `NONE` meanings.
- [x] Evaluate dynamic active and visible values exactly once per root or
  descendant in one classification.
- [x] Change `PointerDispatcher.resolve(root, screen_position)` to delegate to
  the GUI classifier's public `invoke()` method.
- [x] Retain pointer sampling and enter, leave, and update lifecycle ownership
  in `PointerDispatcher.sample()`.
  - [x] `TARGET` assigns `classification.subject` and performs normal lifecycle
    transitions.
  - [x] `BLOCKED` and `MISS` clear the target and perform the existing leave
    behavior when applicable.
  - [x] `UNKNOWN` preserves the current target and emits no enter, leave, or
    update transition.
  - [x] Missing or incomplete pointer coordinates bypass classifier invocation,
    resolve as `MISS`, and retain existing leave behavior.
- [x] Add focused tests for extracted policy parity, one-time dynamic
  evaluation, dispatcher delegation, lifecycle outcomes, and absence of
  duplicate GUI-view classification logic.

Completion criteria:

- [x] GUI-view obstruction behavior exists only in the GUI classifier.
- [x] Existing determinate pointer lifecycle behavior is preserved and
  indeterminate samples are non-transitioning.

## Phase 4: Migrate all direct pointer-classification consumers

Outcome: No service depends on the legacy result enum or per-axis result shape.

- [ ] Migrate tooltip target detection to canonical classifications.
- [ ] Migrate context-menu target detection to canonical classifications.
- [ ] Migrate Input Event UI-obstruction resolution to canonical
  classifications.
- [ ] Update pointer and service-specific tests to use `kind`, `subject`, and
  immutable `local_position`.
- [ ] Retire `PointerResultKind` and legacy result `x` and `y` fields after all
  direct consumers are migrated.
- [ ] Confirm every direct classifier caller uses public `invoke()`.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] No production consumer references `PointerResultKind` or legacy result
  coordinates.
- [ ] Tooltip and context-menu behavior remains unchanged for determinate GUI
  classifications.

## Phase 5: Implement native UI obstruction classification

Outcome: Native widget userdata is classified directly through an isolated,
source-informed compatibility policy without pretending it is a `gui.View`.

- [ ] Add `NativeUiPointerObstructionClassifier` as a
  `PointerObstructionClassifier` subclass.
- [ ] Implement native widget ancestry, visibility, activity, rectangle,
  clipping, and child traversal against userdata.
  - [ ] Treat `GLOBAL_POSITIONING=true` origins as absolute screen coordinates.
  - [ ] Accumulate all other supported origins from parent-relative geometry.
  - [ ] Traverse supported container children in display order.
- [ ] Add an immutable exact-concrete-type registry whose values are existing
  `PointerPolicy` members.
  - [ ] Register the approved native button family as `TARGET`.
  - [ ] Register the approved selection/editing family as `TARGET`.
  - [ ] Register `widget_container`, `widget_columns_container`,
    `widget_params_container`, `widget_rows_container`, and `widget_stack` as
    `PASS`.
  - [ ] Register the approved presentation-only family as `NONE`.
- [ ] Apply exact-type policy before the separate `CAN_KEY_ACTIVATE` `TARGET`
  fallback; do not use inheritance or name-pattern matching for self-policy.
- [ ] For an unregistered object without activation fallback, resolve self as
  `MISS` while traversing descendants only when it exposes the supported
  `widget_container` child interface.
- [ ] Keep exact `TARGET` and `NONE` policies and activation fallback terminal.
- [ ] Map policy and geometry to canonical results.
  - [ ] `TARGET` returns `TARGET` with widget subject and local position only
    when eligible and hit; otherwise `MISS`.
  - [ ] `PASS` traverses children and otherwise returns `MISS`.
  - [ ] `BLOCK` traverses children first, then returns `BLOCKED` with subject
    when its blocking region is hit, otherwise `MISS`.
  - [ ] `NONE` returns `MISS` without descendant traversal.
- [ ] Return `UNKNOWN` when a recognized interactive widget cannot be
  inspected; do not turn unrecognized or merely visible native geometry into
  an obstruction.
- [ ] Add focused tests for absolute and parent-relative positioning, clipping,
  exact registry precedence, activation fallback, every policy mapping,
  `PASS` versus `NONE`, unregistered-container descendants, malformed
  recognized widgets, and unrecognized occupied geometry.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Native userdata is never adapted to a generic view.
- [ ] Recognized interactive native controls obstruct when hit, while
  unrecognized and presentation-only geometry does not become a false hit.
- [ ] Native inspection uncertainty fails closed only for recognized
  interactive widgets.

## Phase 6: Replace UI-root collection with explicit shallow descriptors

Outcome: Current roots are collected without traversal or runtime-type
inference, deduplicated by identity, and dispatched to the correct classifier.

- [ ] Introduce immutable numeric `UiRootKind` members:
  `NATIVE_WIDGET_TREE`, `LUA_VIEW`, `OVERLAY_VIEW`, and
  `CORE_REGISTERED_VIEW`.
- [ ] Introduce immutable tagged root descriptors that retain the original root
  object and explicit kind only for the current input.
- [ ] Collect the current native viewscreen widget root, hooked Lua-screen
  receiver, applicable overlay roots, and existing context/priority-consumer
  roots as explicit Core roots.
- [ ] Keep collection shallow; do not classify or recursively traverse roots
  during collection.
- [ ] Deduplicate roots by object identity.
  - [ ] Resolve duplicate generic Lua kinds with precedence `OVERLAY_VIEW`, then
    `LUA_VIEW`, then `CORE_REGISTERED_VIEW`.
  - [ ] Treat one object reported under incompatible native and Lua kinds as a
    collection-level `UNKNOWN`.
- [ ] Route native descriptors only to the native classifier and all GUI-view
  descriptor kinds only to the GUI classifier.
- [ ] Aggregate root outcomes so `TARGET` or `BLOCKED` wins, then `UNKNOWN`,
  and only all-`MISS` proves unobstructed input.
- [ ] Record distinct diagnostics for collection failure, unsupported kind,
  classifier/traversal failure, applicability failure, and positive
  obstruction without exposing descriptors publicly.
- [ ] Add focused tests for every descriptor kind, shallow collection,
  identity deduplication, kind precedence, incompatible duplicates, explicit
  dispatch, aggregation precedence, immutable descriptors, and per-input
  lifetime.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Test representation cannot alter root semantics because every root kind
  is explicit.
- [ ] All supported roots are classified once through the appropriate public
  classifier boundary.
- [ ] Only a complete all-`MISS` result qualifies as unobstructed.

## Phase 7: Implement the overlay applicability compatibility adapter

Outcome: Root collection includes only overlays applicable to the current input
context while leaving dynamic pointer state to the shared GUI classifier.

- [ ] Add one isolated adapter matching DFHack's overlay-feed viewscreen,
  focus, and enabled predicates.
- [ ] Exclude disabled, viewscreen-inapplicable, and focus-inapplicable overlays
  during root collection.
- [ ] Leave dynamic active, visible, geometry, clipping, traversal, and pointer
  policy evaluation to `GuiViewPointerObstructionClassifier`.
- [ ] Ensure the classifier captures each dynamic active and visible value once
  for the current classification; do not reuse that capture when the overlay
  predecessor independently executes later.
- [ ] Treat failure to inspect an otherwise applicable supported overlay as
  `UNKNOWN`; do not let inapplicable overlays interfere.
- [ ] Add focused compatibility tests for enabled state and representative
  viewscreen/focus transitions, plus malformed applicable overlays.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Collected overlays match the current feed context closely enough that
  inactive contexts neither obstruct nor produce false `UNKNOWN` results.
- [ ] Overlay applicability and pointer classification have separate,
  non-duplicated responsibilities.

## Phase 8: Integrate classification with the existing input trampoline

Outcome: One captured input snapshot and one hook enforce approved RAW,
predecessor, and MAP ordering without resampling or changing public APIs.

- [ ] Capture applicable root descriptors and geometric obstruction once from
  the immutable pre-predecessor `screen_position`.
- [ ] Do not perform a second screen-position or map-position lookup during
  obstruction resolution or after predecessor invocation.
- [ ] Preserve private Core-consumer arbitration before public click delivery.
- [ ] Dispatch eligible `RAW_CLICK` interceptors before the predecessor.
  - [ ] On raw consumption, stop later raw interceptors, notify eligible raw
    observers, skip predecessor and every MAP callback, and return consumed.
- [ ] Invoke the existing overlay-feed predecessor exactly once when raw input
  passes and retain its consumed result.
- [ ] Dispatch eligible `RAW_CLICK` observers after predecessor completion and
  before any MAP callbacks.
- [ ] Suppress every `MAP_CLICK` callback when the predecessor consumed input or
  geometric aggregation is obstructed or `UNKNOWN`.
- [ ] When predecessor and geometry both pass, dispatch `MAP_CLICK`
  interceptors and then observers.
  - [ ] A MAP interceptor may prevent native game delegation but cannot affect
    completed RAW delivery or predecessor processing.
- [ ] Preserve the parent proposal's registration ordering, callback snapshot,
  mutation, recursion, failure containment, and immutable event guarantees.
- [ ] Ensure obstruction uncertainty suppresses only the current `MAP_CLICK`
  and does not make the service unhealthy or suppress an eligible `RAW_CLICK`.
- [ ] Add focused tests for exact ordering, predecessor consumption, RAW and MAP
  consumption, all-mouse-input eligibility, obstruction aggregation, no
  resampling, observer timing, inherited return behavior, and failure
  isolation.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] One physical mouse-input boundary produces the approved RAW/predecessor/
  MAP sequence through the existing trampoline.
- [ ] RAW consumption prevents MAP and all later host handling; MAP consumption
  occurs only after overlays decline input and prevents native delegation.
- [ ] Root resolution never changes otherwise eligible RAW delivery.

## Phase 9: Complete reload, registry, packaging, and documentation migration

Outcome: The redesigned modules participate correctly in reload/package
boundaries and the retired adaptation/result contracts are absent.

- [ ] Register new production modules in `dwarfuicore/module_registry.lua` in
  dependency order and update registry/package declaration tests.
- [ ] Ensure classifier modules and root descriptors follow generation and
  reload ownership while per-input descriptors never survive reload.
- [ ] Preserve the established service generation, hook adoption, stale-handle,
  and owned-cleanup behavior.
- [ ] Remove the provisional native-to-generic-view workaround and every
  superseded UI-root adaptation path.
- [ ] Remove obsolete legacy pointer-result declarations and compatibility
  exports after consumers are migrated.
- [ ] Update contributor documentation with supported root kinds, classifier
  extension rules, native compatibility-policy requirements, and fail-closed
  behavior.
- [ ] Keep public documentation focused on event semantics, including RAW's
  lack of UI guarantee and MAP's post-overlay/pre-native boundary.
- [ ] Update exact expanded/archive package expectations for all added and
  removed modules.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Reload and packaging contain one current classifier/root-resolution
  architecture with no adaptation workaround or legacy result shape.
- [ ] Public API, hook ownership, and generation behavior remain unchanged.

## Phase 10: Focused and regression qualification

Outcome: Source and unit evidence demonstrate the redesigned contracts without
conflating them with native-runtime behavior.

- [ ] Run focused unit suites for positions, canonical results, classifier
  invocation, GUI extraction, dispatcher lifecycle, native policy, root
  collection, overlay compatibility, aggregation, and trampoline ordering.
- [ ] Run tooltip, context-menu, UserPrompt, Input Event, provider, module
  registry, reload, and package regression suites.
- [ ] Run the complete DwarfUICore unit suite.
- [ ] Run Lua syntax and source-declaration validation for production and test
  modules.
- [ ] Build the distributable package and verify exact expanded and archive
  contents separately.
- [ ] Record focused, regression, full-unit, syntax/source, and package results
  as distinct evidence.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Every required source and unit boundary passes with separately recorded
  results.
- [ ] Any failed or unavailable evidence remains unchecked and is not presented
  as runtime qualification.

## Phase 11: DwarfSpec automation qualification

Outcome: Native runtime automation qualifies geometric classification,
consumption ordering, reload behavior, and cleanup on supported input surfaces.

- [ ] Run native-overlay automation proving unobstructed input emits RAW and
  MAP, while recognized native, Lua, and overlay obstructions emit RAW only.
- [ ] Qualify representative registered native button and selection/editing
  controls as MAP obstructions.
- [ ] Qualify representative structural, presentation-only, and unrecognized
  native geometry as non-obstructing when no recognized interactive descendant
  is hit.
- [ ] Qualify `GLOBAL_POSITIONING` as absolute screen space and ordinary native
  widget positioning as parent-relative.
- [ ] Qualify visible DFHack elements with `PASS` or `NONE` as non-obstructing
  and `TARGET` or `BLOCKED` as obstructing.
- [ ] Qualify overlay viewscreen/focus applicability and overlay-predecessor
  consumption independently from geometric obstruction.
- [ ] Qualify mouse inputs beyond left/right through the same event contract;
  do not add tests for nonexistent host event types.
- [ ] Qualify exact interception/observation ordering.
  - [ ] RAW consumption prevents predecessor invocation, MAP delivery, and
    native game delegation.
  - [ ] MAP consumption occurs after overlays decline input and prevents native
    game delegation.
- [ ] Run equivalent supported Lua-screen automation.
- [ ] Run installed-package automation separately from source-checkout
  automation.
- [ ] Run reload automation proving one runtime, one hook chain, classifier
  availability, stale-generation rejection, and no retained root descriptors.
- [ ] Record terminal cleanup evidence proving temporary subscriptions, UI,
  hooks, and runtime state are removed or returned to their intended inert
  state without changing reload behavior.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Native-overlay, Lua-screen, installed-package, reload, and cleanup results
  are recorded independently with terminal status.
- [ ] Native interaction and positioning assumptions have representative
  runtime evidence rather than unit-test inference alone.
- [ ] Any unavailable or failed runtime contract remains unchecked.

## Final acceptance

- [ ] Every supported root has an explicit immutable root kind and reaches the
  correct classifier through public `invoke()`.
- [ ] GUI pointer obstruction has one implementation shared by Input Event and
  `PointerDispatcher`; continuous lifecycle remains owned by the dispatcher.
- [ ] Native userdata is traversed directly using the approved exact-type
  `PointerPolicy` registry, activation fallback, and structural fallback.
- [ ] Unrecognized native UI does not become an interaction hit solely from
  visibility or geometry; recognized uninspectable interaction surfaces become
  `UNKNOWN`.
- [ ] Canonical classifications use `kind`, neutral `subject`, and immutable
  `local_position`; legacy kinds and per-axis result fields are removed.
- [ ] Missing pointer coordinates produce determinate `MISS` before classifier
  invocation; classifier uncertainty produces non-transitioning continuous
  behavior and fail-closed MAP behavior.
- [ ] Root collection is shallow, identity-deduplicated, per-input, and rejects
  incompatible native/Lua duplicate kinds as `UNKNOWN`.
- [ ] Overlay applicability mirrors current input context while dynamic
  pointer state remains classifier-owned and captured once per classification.
- [ ] One existing trampoline captures once, dispatches RAW before predecessor
  and MAP after predecessor, and never resamples coordinates.
- [ ] RAW consumption prevents MAP and host delegation; predecessor consumption
  suppresses MAP; MAP consumption prevents only later native delegation.
- [ ] Public provider methods, payload semantics, namespace/handle contracts,
  hook ownership, reload behavior, and service health rules remain unchanged.
- [ ] Every proposal requirement is implemented or explicitly deferred with an
  approved rationale.
- [ ] Required source, unit, package, DwarfSpec, reload, and cleanup evidence is
  complete and recorded as distinct proof boundaries.
